// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// agent/domains/CHAT/akida_sw_lif.hexa — WRAPPER doc-stub
//
//   akida_sw_lif.py is the numpy LIF software simulator that mirrors
//   akida.FullyConnected(units=N).forward(): integer threshold-and-fire
//   (potential = Σ_i clip(x_i,0,15); spike iff potential > threshold[j]).
//   It is the SW fallback used by substrate_akida.py when no BrainChip
//   AKD1000 is reachable. seed=187 deterministic; reproduces the R0..R4
//   regimes of SUB_ENGINES/AKIDA/scripts/spontaneous_emission.py.
//
//   It hard-depends on numpy (vectorised int compare over the neuron pool)
//   — a pure-hexa reimplementation duplicates the canonical raster spec
//   for no gain. The .py is KEPT as the runnable simulator and is imported
//   by substrate_akida.py (SW path), never run standalone — this .hexa is
//   the hexa-native marker recording the deliberate WRAPPER verdict.
//
//   HW-SW calibration loop round 1 (2026-05-29): the .py per-regime record was
//   extended to emit the SAME derived statistics as the on-chip script
//   (isi_min/isi_max + first10/last10 rasters + wall_ms_per_step), so HW-vs-SW
//   is now diffable on the FULL distribution surface. A live-silicon step-by-step
//   replay (seed=187, n=16, 200 steps) showed the SW R2 raster is BYTE-IDENTICAL
//   to the AKD1000 raster, and the HW is deterministic across runs (no analog
//   jitter at this seed) — convergence-target dims (rate/std/saturation/ISI)
//   already fully converged; this round closed the reporting-surface gap.
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 3 (2026-05-30): added fc_quantized_forward() — the
//   act_bits>1 / non-ones-weight GENERALIZATION of lif_forward. The frontier
//   sweep recovered the real AKD1000 activation quantizer on silicon:
//     potential_j = Σ_i x_i·W_ij ; y = clip(ceil(potential/step), 0, 2^ab-1)
//     step = 2^(input_bits - act_bits)  [ab=4→1, ab=2→4, ab=1→8 = lif comparator]
//   plus SYMMETRIC int weights [-7,+7] (chip rejects -8). Verified BYTE-IDENTICAL
//   to HW across act_bits{1,2,4} × {all-ones, random int4} × {1,2 layers} (80/80
//   probe inputs, max Hamming 0). act_bits=1+ones reduces EXACTLY to lif_forward
//   so verify_substrate_akida stays 5/5. CLOSED-NEGATIVE: on-chip
//   AkidaUnsupervised LEARNING is non-deterministic (hidden plasticity state,
//   same-init+same-input → different fitted weights) and is NOT modeled here.
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 4 (2026-05-30): added cascade_forward() — the >=3-layer
//   GENERALIZATION of chaining fc_quantized_forward over a list of weight
//   tensors (each layer's quantized output feeds the next). Verified
//   BYTE-IDENTICAL to the AKD1000 N-stacked FullyConnected for L in {3,4},
//   act_bits {2,4}, random symmetric int4 (max Hamming 0) — the per-layer
//   quantizer composes exactly with no depth-dependent HW drift. L=1/2 reduce
//   to the round-3 single/2-layer chain so verify_substrate_akida stays 5/5.
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 4 conv (2026-05-30): added conv2d_quantized_forward() —
//   quantized 2-D conv (SAME pad, stride 1) + the SAME activation quantizer as FC.
//   AKD1000 splits conv into TWO layer types (recovered by impulse probe on
//   silicon): InputConvolutional = akida SW front-end, CROSS-CORRELATION
//   (flip=False); Convolutional = on-chip CNP (genuine HW), TRUE CONVOLUTION =
//   180deg kernel flip (flip=True). Verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to AKD1000 for
//   InputConv->Conv cascades (act_bits 4, sym int4, F<=8, K=3), max Hamming 0.
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 5 stride/VALID (2026-05-30): conv2d_quantized_forward()
//   gained a `stride` param + TF SAME/VALID geometry (round 4 was stride1 SAME
//   only). SAME: oh=ceil(H/s), asymmetric pad (extra to bottom/right); VALID:
//   no pad, oh=floor((H-K)/s)+1. Verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to AKD1000 for
//   InputConv->Conv stride{2}xSAME and stride{1,2}xVALID, max Hamming 0.
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 5 pooling (2026-05-30): added pool2d_quantized_forward().
//   AKD1000 fuses pooling INTO the Conv layer (pool_size/pool_type/pool_stride;
//   no standalone pool layer). MAX pool = EXTENDED+verified: windowed max over
//   the quantized activations; since the quantizer is monotone, max-after-act ==
//   the chip's fused Conv+MaxPool -> 10/10 byte-identical (2x2 s2, ab4, F8, K3).
//   AVERAGE/GLOBAL pool = CLOSED-NEGATIVE: AKD1000 average is GLOBAL only
//   (pool_size=-1), runs on the akida SW backend with a DETERMINISTIC but opaque
//   per-channel rescale that is NOT a function of the public activation-map mean
//   (per-channel sweep: non-monotone, smaller act-sum -> larger pooled output);
//   not recoverable from weights+activation -> refused (raises NotImplementedError).
//
//   HW-SW FRONTIER round 5 sepconv (2026-05-30): added sepconv2d_quantized_forward()
//   for SeparableConvolutional (depthwise then pointwise). RECOVERED on silicon:
//   the chip FUSES depthwise + pointwise -- depthwise is a TRUE convolution
//   (180deg flip) over RAW potentials with NO intermediate activation, fed
//   straight into the pointwise 1x1 accumulation, with a SINGLE activation
//   quantizer at the end. A naive two-quantizer (dw-act then pw-act) diverges by
//   >100 Hamming; the chip quantizes ONCE. Verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to AKD1000
//   InputConv->SeparableConv (act_bits {2,4}, sym int4, Cin=4 F=8 K=3, SAME),
//   20/20 probes, max Hamming 0.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn main() {
    println("akida_sw_lif.py — numpy LIF sim (akida.FullyConnected.forward mirror).")
    println("Imported by substrate_akida.py SW fallback path; not standalone.")
}
